# Scala Native's process-global unsafe memory pool retains its first chunk at
# shutdown unless the full AddressSanitizer mode is active. Suppress only its
# allocation site; allocations made by xkafka and librdkafka remain visible.
leak:_SM35scala.scalanative.unsafe.MemoryPoolD13allocateChunk

# OpenSSL keeps a per-thread random generator that librdkafka creates when it
# asks for random bytes, such as for a consumer group's id, and frees it when
# that thread exits. The check reports it at exit on some runs and not on
# others. Suppress only what is allocated under librdkafka's call into
# OpenSSL's generator.
leak:rd_rand_bytes_by_ossl
